Hiragi: (I never look inside. I never come close to understanding what he's actually carrying.)
Hiragi: (Bit by bit, without either of us really noticing, a wall goes up between us. Nothing dramatic — just a few more unanswered texts, a few more excuses not to walk home together.)
Hiragi: (He never finds out if I looked and said nothing, or truly never wanted to know — and he never asks. He keeps the smile on and lets everything else quietly fall apart where I can't see it.)
